<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 639 0 R
/E (The Food Ordering and Delivery System is a digital platform that enables customers to order food online from various restaurants and have it delivered to their location. The system connects customers, restaurant staff, delivery drivers, and administrators into a single integrated environment that supports real-time communication and efficient service management.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
816 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 639 0 R
/E (Through the platform, customers can browse restaurant menus, select food items, place orders, and complete secure online payments. Once an order is submitted, the restaurant receives it instantly and begins preparation. After the order is ready, a delivery driver is assigned to pick up and deliver the food to the customer. The system also allows users to track the status of their orders in real time.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
817 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 639 0 R
/E (The platform supports multiple user roles, each with specific functionalities. Customers interact with the ordering interface, restaurant staff manage menus and orders, delivery drivers handle deliveries, and administrators oversee system operations. In addition, the system integrates with external services such as payment gateways and notification systems to ensure secure transactions and timely updates.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
